version: 1
document:
  title: Creators LICENCE (Build on MultiBuild License)
  version: 2025-12-19
  date: 2025-12-19
  copyright:
    year: 2025
    author: Multiboard LTD
    company-number: 15578423
    url: https://multibuild.io/license
  uuid: fae87a17-e094-42df-91ce-d7375ae51230
  glossary: https://glossary.object-notation-environment.github.com
  source:
    summary-page: https://multibuild.io/license
    full-legal-code: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1C0-Iyxydqk_d2I3o_5ualJ9Ywt9gwVdl9eukvC8JeKA/
    retrieved: 2026-08-29
    contact: hello@MultiBuild.io
    note: |
      A verbatim port of the full legal code into SYON. Nothing is
      paraphrased, reordered or renumbered. The published document numbers
      two consecutive sections 4 -- CANCELLATION OF YOUR LICENCE and YOUR
      OBLIGATIONS -- and ends with two empty numbered items; both are
      preserved as published rather than corrected here, since a port that
      tidies a legal document is no longer a copy of it.

      This licence covers 3D design files and the physical parts made from
      them. It is not a software licence, it grants no permission to reuse
      the text of the licence itself, and it is revocable by Multiboard LTD.
      Its presence in this repository is a record of the document, not a
      grant of rights over anything in this repository.

content:
    notice: |
        Please read the following important terms and conditions before
        using, downloading, copying or modifying any MultiBuild 3D design
        files or any other material (including but not limited to designs,
        drawings, documentation and manuals or downloadable files) which are
        owned or licensed by Multiboard LTD (Designs) and check that they
        contain everything you want and nothing that you are not willing to
        agree to.

    summary:
        type: chapter
        style: capitalized
        numbered: 0
        title: Plain English Summary (for convenience only)
        note: |
            This summary is provided to help explain the key points of the
            licence. It does not replace or override the full legal terms
            below.
        text:
            - You can download and use MultiBuild designs for personal, non-commercial use.
            - If you want to sell physical products made from the designs, you need a Commercial Subscription.
            - Commercial sales are capped at $50,000 USD per year unless a separate licence is agreed.
            - |
              You may remix the designs. You own your original contributions,
              but you do not own the underlying MultiBuild designs.
            - You may not redistribute the original design files.
            - |
              You may not bundle, collect, or redistribute MultiBuild designs
              outside the MultiBuild platform, including creating or sharing
              large link collections or external repositories of designs.
            - Mass-manufacturing methods such as injection moulding are not permitted.
            - MultiBuild is not responsible for how you manufacture, install, or use printed parts.
        closing: |
            Please read the following important terms and conditions, if there
            is any inconsistency between this summary and the full licence,
            the full licence prevails.

    how-these-terms-work:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 0
        title: HOW THESE TERMS WORK
        text:
            - |
              These terms and conditions (Terms) apply if you are using,
              downloading, copying, modifying (Using, Use) the Designs. These
              Terms apply in addition to, and should be read together with,
              the terms of Thangs.com, available here:
              https://thangs.com/terms-and-conditions (Thangs Terms).
            - |
              To the extent of any inconsistency between the Thangs Terms and
              these Terms, these Terms shall prevail.
            - |
              In these Terms, capitalised words and phrases have the meanings
              given to them where they are followed by bolded brackets, or as
              set out in the Definitions table at the end of these Terms.
            - |
              By Using a Design, you agree to be bound by these Terms which
              form a binding contractual agreement between you the person
              acquiring a Subscription or Design, or the company you represent
              and are acquiring the Subscription or Design on behalf of
              (‘you’ or ‘your’) and us, MultiBoard LTD (MultiBuild, we, us,
              our).
            - |
              We may change these Terms at any time by notifying you via our
              community announcement channel, and your continued use of the
              Designs following such an update will represent an agreement by
              you to be bound by the Terms as amended.

    eligibility:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 1
        title: ELIGIBILITY
        clauses:
            - |
              By accepting these Terms, you represent and warrant that you
              have the legal capacity and authority to enter into a binding
              contract with us.
            - |
              Please do not Use the Designs if you are under the age of 18
              years old and do not have your parent or guardian’s consent, if
              you are under 16 or if you have previously been suspended or
              prohibited from using the Software.
            - |
              If you are Using the Designs not as an individual but on behalf
              of your company, your employer, an organisation, government or
              other legal entity (Represented Entity), then “you” or “your”
              means the Represented Entity and you are binding the Represented
              Entity to this agreement. If you are accepting this agreement
              and using our Designs on behalf of a Represented Entity, you
              represent and warrant that you are authorised to do so.

    subscriptions:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 2
        title: SUBSCRIPTIONS
        sections:
            subscriptions-and-accounts:
                numbered: 2.1
                title: SUBSCRIPTIONS AND ACCOUNTS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      To Use our Downloads, you may be required to sign up for
                      an account with Thangs.com (Account) and pay for a
                      subscription (Subscription).
                    - |
                      We offer different tiers of Subscriptions (Subscription
                      Tiers) as set out on the Thangs platform here
                      https://thangs.com/designer/MultiBuild (Platform).
                    - |
                      We reserve the right to offer Designs on an exclusive
                      basis to certain Subscription Tiers, or allow certain
                      Subscription Tiers early access to our Designs, as set
                      out on the Platform.
                    - |
                      You may only Use the Designs as a consumer for Personal
                      Use unless otherwise agreed by us in writing.
                    - |
                      If you are Using the Designed Works in the course of
                      business to derive income of any kind including without
                      limitation to sell any Designed Works, you must have a
                      Multipartner subscription.
                    - |
                      Your Use of the Designs is subject to the licence granted
                      to your Subscription Tier, as set out in clause 3.
            disclaimer:
                numbered: 2.2
                title: DISCLAIMER
                lead: You acknowledge and agree that:
                clauses:
                    - |
                      any information provided to you as part of or in
                      connection with the Designs is general in nature, may not
                      be suitable for your circumstances and does not
                      constitute financial, legal or any other kind of
                      professional advice;
                    - |
                      we make no warranties as to the suitability of the
                      Designs or any Designed Works for your use, and you are
                      solely responsible for the material and production of
                      Designed Works. Any weight limits or suggestions for
                      materials and production are general and not professional
                      advice, and you should use care when installing and using
                      any Designed Works; and
                    - |
                      it is your responsibility to comply with applicable laws
                      relevant to your Use of the Designs (including but not
                      limited to your business, including industrial relations
                      Laws and privacy laws).
            designs:
                numbered: 2.3
                title: DESIGNS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      We may from time to time, in our absolute discretion,
                      release enhancements to the Designs, meaning an upgraded,
                      improved, modified or new versions of the Designs
                      (Enhancements). Any Enhancements to the Designs will not
                      limit or otherwise affect these Terms.
                    - We may change any features of the Designs at any time.
            service-limitations:
                numbered: 2.4
                title: SERVICE LIMITATIONS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      The Designs are made available to you strictly on an
                      ‘as is’ basis. Without limitation we do not guarantee
                      that:
                      1. the Designs will be free from errors or defects;
                      2. the Designs will be accessible at all times; or
                      3. any information provided with the Designs is accurate
                         or true.
                    - |
                      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, all
                      express or implied representations and warranties
                      (whether relating to fitness for purpose or performance,
                      or otherwise) not expressly stated in this agreement are
                      excluded.

    intellectual-property-license:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 3
        title: INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY LICENSE
        sections:
            definitions:
                numbered: 3.1
                title: DEFINITIONS
                lead: In these Terms:
                terms:
                    Commercial Subscription: |
                        means the Multi Partner membership plan on the
                        Platform;
                    Commercial Sale: |
                        means the sale of Designed Works that generates gross
                        revenue exceeding $100 USD per calendar month for three
                        (3) consecutive months, calculated per individual or
                        legal entity, before tax and expenses.
                    Designed Works: means any physical product produced or derived from a Design;
                    Intellectual Property Rights: |
                        means any and all present and future intellectual and
                        industrial property rights throughout the world
                        (whether registered or unregistered), including
                        copyright, trade marks, designs, patents, moral rights,
                        semiconductor and circuit layout rights, trade,
                        business, company and domain names, and other
                        proprietary rights, trade secrets, know-how, technical
                        data, confidential information and the right to have
                        information kept confidential, or any rights to
                        registration of such rights (including renewal),
                        whether created before or after the date of this
                        agreement; and
                    Remixed Design: |
                        means a derivative, modified, adapted or enhanced
                        version of the Designs.
                    Personal Use: |
                        means non-commercial use that does not generate direct
                        revenue from Designed Works, including but not limited
                        to sale, licensing, advertising, or paid access.
                    Substantial change: |
                        means a modification that results in a material and
                        objectively identifiable difference from the original
                        Design, including a material change to its geometry,
                        function, or intended use, such that a reasonable and
                        technically competent third party would not regard the
                        original Design as the primary basis of the Remixed
                        Design.
            design-license:
                numbered: 3.2
                title: DESIGN LICENSE
                clauses:
                    - |
                      We grant you a revocable, worldwide, royalty-free,
                      non-transferrable (and non-sublicensable, except as
                      contemplated by clause 3.3) license to use the
                      Intellectual Property in the Designs for:
                      1. your Personal Use only, including making Designed
                         Works for your Personal Use. For the avoidance of
                         doubt, any activity constituting a Commercial Sale
                         requires a Commercial Subscription; and
                      2. If you hold a Commercial Subscription, commercial
                         purposes subject to clause 3.2(b).
                    - |
                      For the avoidance of doubt, you are not permitted to use
                      the Designs for any injection moulding purpose, including
                      but not limited to building the Designs using injection
                      moulding or similar techniques, excluding layer-by-layer
                      additive manufacturing methods such as Fused Filament
                      Fabrication (FFF), also known as 3D printing,
                      Stereolithography (SLA).
                    - |
                      Commercial Subscription holders are permitted under this
                      license to use the Intellectual Property in the Designs,
                      including without limitation the Designs themselves:
                      1. Solely for the purpose of making Designed Works which
                         may be sold on a commercial basis subject to clause
                         3.2(b)(ii), and not to license or sublicense any part
                         of the Designs; and
                      2. the Designed Works may be sold up to a maximum of
                         $50,000 USD per annum in total sales for the Designed
                         Works (Sales Cap).
                    - |
                      You must not exceed the Sales Cap under your Commercial
                      Subscription without our prior consent. You will exceed
                      the Sales Cap if you earn or generate gross revenue
                      before tax from the sale of Designed Works, calculated on
                      a rolling 12-month basis, per legal entity or individual.

                      For the avoidance of doubt, gross revenue includes all
                      amounts invoiced or received, whether directly or
                      indirectly, and whether or not a profit is made.

                      If you exceed the Sales Cap you must obtain an additional
                      commercial license, subject to our agreement. Please
                      contact us at hello@MultiBuild.io to discuss commercial
                      license options. If you do not obtain an additional
                      commercial license, you must cease production and sales
                      of the Designed Works.
                    - |
                      If you cease to hold a Commercial Subscription, you must
                      cease all sales of any Designed Works.
                    - |
                      If you breach any terms or conditions of your license set
                      out in this clause 3, you acknowledge and agree:
                      1. That MultiBoard LTD may terminate your subscription
                         and the license granted to you under these Terms; and
                      2. You indemnify us for any loss, damage, claim, expense
                         or cost we suffer or incur as a result of your breach.
                    - |
                      For the avoidance of doubt, nothing in these terms gives
                      you any ownership rights in respect of Remixed Designs.
                      Remixed Designs are the product of both MultiBoard LTD
                      and third party Intellectual Property Rights, and
                      therefore you must obtain any required third-party
                      consents before you can use the Remixed Designs.
            remixed-designs:
                numbered: 3.3
                title: REMIXED DESIGNS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      Under this licence you may adapt and modify the Designs
                      to create Remixed Designs provided:
                      1. The Remixed Designs must be a substantial change from
                         the original Designs;
                      2. You must not share, publish, distribute, sell, loan,
                         or make available to the public or any individual or
                         entity the original Designs;
                      3. To the extent that the Designs form part of the
                         Remixed Designs, they may only be licensed or
                         sublicensed as part of the Remixed Designs subject to
                         the same conditions under which the original Designs
                         are licensed under these Terms, and we encourage you
                         to adopt the same license terms in respect of the
                         Remixed Designs as a whole;
                      4. The Remixed Designs must not infringe any Intellectual
                         Property Rights, including copyright, trademarks,
                         business names, patents, Confidential Information or
                         any other similar proprietary rights, whether
                         registered or unregistered, anywhere in the world;
                      5. The Remixed Designs must not breach or infringe any
                         laws or regulations including being created for the
                         purpose of any illegal purpose;
                      6. The Remixed Designs must not contain any viruses or
                         other harmful code, or otherwise compromise the
                         security or integrity of any network or system; and
                      7. You and the Remixed Designs comply at all times with
                         clause 4.
                    - |
                      You grant to MultiBoard LTD a non-exclusive, royalty
                      free, non-transferable, sub-licensable, worldwide and
                      irrevocable licence to use, including without limitation
                      adapt, modify and enhance the Remixed Designs.
                    - |
                      You:
                      1. Warrant that MultiBoard LTD’s use of the Remixed
                         Designs as contemplated by this agreement will not
                         infringe any third-party Intellectual Property Rights;
                         and
                      2. indemnify MultiBoard LTD from and against all losses,
                         claims, expenses, damages and liabilities (including
                         any taxes, fees or costs) which arise out of such
                         infringement.
                    - |
                      We reserve the right to terminate the right to create
                      Remixed Designs under this license in our reasonable
                      discretion, including without limitation if we believe
                      you to be misusing the license.
            cancellation-of-your-licence:
                numbered: 3.4
                title: CANCELLATION OF YOUR LICENCE
                note: |
                    Numbered 4 in the published document, which numbers the
                    next chapter 4 as well. Preserved as published.
                clauses:
                    - |
                      We reserve the right to terminate your license granted
                      under these Terms without notice to you if you have
                      breached any part of these Terms.

    your-obligations:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 4
        title: YOUR OBLIGATIONS
        clauses:
            - |
              You must comply with these Terms at all times. You acknowledge
              and agree that we will have no liability in respect of any
              damage, loss or expense which arises in connection with your
              breach of these Terms, and you indemnify us in respect of any
              such damage, loss or expense.
            - |
              You must not, and must not encourage or permit any employee,
              agent, officer or contractor (Personnel) or any third party to,
              without our prior written approval:
              1. use the Designs in any illegal, unsafe, misleading, or harmful
                 manner, including any use that is illegal or fraudulent or
                 that facilitates illegal or fraudulent activity;
              2. make copies of the Designs;
              3. adapt, modify or tamper in any way with the Designs, other
                 than as permitted under these Terms;
              4. remove or alter any copyright, trade mark or other notice on
                 or forming part of the Designs;
              5. You must not make false or misleading statements that
                 reasonably imply endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation by
                 us.
              6. use the Designs in a way which infringes the Intellectual
                 Property Rights of any third party;
              7. create derivative works from or translate the Designs, other
                 than as permitted under these Terms;
              8. publish or otherwise communicate the Designs to the public,
                 including by making it available online or sharing it with
                 third parties;
              9. intimidate, harass, impersonate, stalk, threaten, bully or
                 endanger any other User or distribute unsolicited commercial
                 content, junk mail, spam, bulk content or harassment in
                 connection with the Designs; or
              10. sell, loan, transfer, sub-licence, hire or otherwise dispose
                  of the Designs (or any Designed Works or Remixed Designs) to
                  any third party, except as permitted under these Terms;
              11. create, maintain, share, publish, or distribute any external
                  collection, bundle, pack, index, or repository of Designs or
                  links to Designs, whether free or paid, where such collection
                  contains more than 100 links, files, or references to
                  Designs, or is intended to replicate, substitute for, or
                  circumvent access to the Designs through the Platform.

              For the avoidance of doubt, this does not prevent reasonable,
              incidental linking to individual Designs for discussion, review,
              or educational purposes.
            - |
              If you become aware of misuse of the Designs by any person, any
              errors in the material of the Designs or any difficulty in
              accessing or using your Subscription or the Designs, please
              contact us immediately by email to hello@MultiBuild.io
            - |
              You must not represent, claim, or imply that any Designed Works
              are your own original designs.

              In the case of Remixed Designs, you may represent your original
              contributions as your own, provided that you do not misrepresent
              the origin of the underlying MultiBuild Designs or present the
              Remixed Designs in a manner that is likely to cause confusion as
              to the source of the underlying system or core design elements.

              Where practicable, public publications or showcases of Designed
              Works or Remixed Designs should include attribution to
              MultiBoard LTD as the source of the underlying designs.
            - |
              You agree:
              1. to comply with each of your obligations in these Terms;
              2. that information given to you through the Subscription or
                 Designs, by us or another User, is general in nature and we
                 take no responsibility for anything caused by any actions you
                 take in reliance on that information; and
              3. that we may cancel your, or any User’s, Account at any time if
                 we consider, in our absolute discretion, that you or they are
                 in breach of, or are likely to breach, this clause.

    liability-and-indemnity:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 5
        title: LIABILITY AND INDEMNITY
        clauses:
            - |
              (Liability) To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law,
              MultiBoard LTD limits all liability in aggregate of all claims to
              you (and any third parties who encounter the Designs or Designed
              Works through your business) for loss or damage of any kind,
              however arising whether in contract, tort, statute, equity,
              indemnity or otherwise, arising from or relating in any way to
              this agreement or any goods or services provided by MultiBoard
              LTD to £100.
            - |
              (Indemnity) You indemnify MultiBoard LTD and its employees,
              contractors and agents in respect of all liability for any
              claim(s) by any person (including any third party who encounter
              the Designs or Designed Works through your business) arising from
              your, or your employee’s, client’s, contractor’s or agent’s:
              1. breach of any third party intellectual property rights;
              2. breach of these Terms;
              3. negligent, wilful, fraudulent or criminal act or omission; or
              4. use of the Designs.
            - |
              (Consequential loss) To the maximum extent permitted by law,
              under no circumstances will MultiBoard LTD be liable for any
              incidental, special or consequential loss or damages, or damages
              for loss of data, business or business opportunity, goodwill,
              anticipated savings, profits or revenue arising under or in
              connection with this agreement or any goods or services provided
              by MultiBoard LTD.
            - |
              (Unfair Contract Terms) To the extent that the provisions of any
              applicable law shall impose restrictions on the extent to which
              liability can be excluded under these including, for the
              avoidance of doubt, the provisions of sections 3, 6 and 11 of the
              Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 in the UK (and its equivalent in
              any other jurisdiction) relating to the requirement of
              reasonableness, the exclusions set out in this clause shall be
              limited in accordance with such restrictions. However, any
              exclusions of liability that are not affected by such
              restrictions shall remain in full force and effect.
            - |
              Nothing in this agreement shall exclude or limit a party’s
              liability for fraud or intentional unlawful conduct by a party,
              or death or personal injury resulting from a party’s negligence.

    general:
        type: chapter
        style: upper case
        numbered: 6
        title: GENERAL
        sections:
            governing-law-and-jurisdiction:
                numbered: 6.1
                title: GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION
                clauses:
                    - |
                      These Terms are governed by the law applying in England
                      and Wales. Each party irrevocably submits to the
                      exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales
                      and courts of appeal from them in respect of any
                      proceedings arising out of or in connection with this
                      agreement. Each party irrevocably waives any objection to
                      the venue of any legal process on the basis that the
                      process has been brought in an inconvenient forum.
            third-party-rights:
                numbered: 6.2
                title: THIRD PARTY RIGHTS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      These Terms do not give rise to any rights under the
                      Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999 to enforce
                      any term of these Terms.
            waiver:
                numbered: 6.3
                title: WAIVER
                clauses:
                    - |
                      No party to this agreement may rely on the words or
                      conduct of any other party as a waiver of any right
                      unless the waiver is in writing and signed by the party
                      granting the waiver.
            further-acts-and-documents:
                numbered: 6.4
                title: FURTHER ACTS AND DOCUMENTS
                clauses:
                    - |
                      Each party must promptly do all further acts and execute
                      and deliver all further documents required by law or
                      reasonably requested by another party to give effect to
                      this agreement.
            assignment:
                numbered: 6.5
                title: ASSIGNMENT
                clauses:
                    - |
                      You can’t assign, novate or otherwise transfer your
                      rights or obligations under this agreement without the
                      MultiBoard LTD’s prior consent.

    trailing-empty-items:
        note: |
            The published document ends with two numbered items, 2 and 3, that
            carry no text. They are recorded here because they are part of the
            document as published, and a reader comparing this port against
            the source should not have to wonder whether something was lost.
        items:
            - 2
            - 3
